istasteful phatphobic  trends of the y2k era so think about the  fat girl trope in popular culture like  shallow hal bridget jones diary monica  on friends and even part of the regina  george character arc in mean girls the  late 90s and early 2000s were cruel as  for people in larger bodies and i do not  want us ever to regress to that point  but we don't have to let it we can  resist censorship by letting these  platforms know that we do not approve  and that we want to see more diverse  bodies and diverse representation of  trends in our feeds so here's a project  for you guys please go follow plus size  creators like and comment on their  content tell the instagram gods that you  want to see more real bodies just  wearing the clothes they love whether  you choose to rock the low-rise jean or  stick to your high-rise like i  definitely will be you should feel  empowered to see  your body represented online  and on that note folks that's all that i  have for you guys today if you liked it  be sure to give it the thumbs up leave  me a comment below on your thoughts on  the low rise jean trend subscribe to the  channel and i'll see you next time on  abby's kitchen bye  [Music]

